{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Fill your hands today to YHWH.</b> Acquire perfection for your hands today, so that they may be prepared to serve Him in His sanctuary." "<b>For each man in his son and in his brother.</b> For each of you has already been consecrated to YHWH — in his son, through the circumcision you performed in the wilderness, and in his brother, through the killing this day. Therefore fill your hands with good intention and complete your preparation for YHWH for His service." "<b>And to bestow upon you today a blessing.</b> And fill your hands as well in such manner that HaShem, blessed be He, may bestow upon you today a blessing — and this is that your aim be to observe His ordinance and His covenant, as it says: כִּי שָׁמְרוּ אִמְרָתֶךָ וּבְרִיתְךָ יִנְצֹרוּ, יוֹרוּ מִשְׁפָּטֶיךָ (Deuteronomy 33:9–10); בָּרֵךְ ה' חֵילוֹ וּפֹעַל יָדָיו תִּרְצֶה (Deuteronomy 33:11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:50.140039375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}